        "id": 71041,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-15T15:04:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was thinking of something a little different. First, figure out what number you are trying to target. Let's say 3. So you want to see how many 3s o 4s are left in the deck. Since there are 21 total, use damage tokens to put 21 by your character. Every time you draw a 3 or 4, subtract 1 token. While you can always just count your cards, this will give you a quick look as to how many are left. If you want a more precise number and percentage, count of the cards in the deck and just divide to find your chance of drawing a 3 or 4.</p>",
